      "reason": "A signed public kind-1 post traversed the actual PWA bridge from R1 to R2. Buyer B saw the author, and the contact action selected that author in private-message navigation while the post remained public."
    },
    {
      "case": "G06-02",
      "status": "PASS",
      "reason": "The browser published, discovered, and edited one satoshi, one piconero, and one raw through two actual Geode relays and a real PWA bridge. Exact atomic strings, event authorship, stable d tags, signatures, and rendered prices survived each round-trip; currency maxima and overflow were checked."
    },
    {
      "case": "G06-03",
      "status": "PASS",
      "reason": "Seller withdrawal hid the offer even after the older signed event was replayed to R2. Geode rejected reinsertion under its deletion tombstone. Another author could not remove an offer; the client reducer ignored an older deletion timestamp without sending that fixture to the relay."
    },
    {
      "case": "G06-04",
      "status": "PASS",
      "reason": "Expired and future-timestamp, unknown-currency, malformed, and ambiguous-address listings were filtered. The browser blocked excess precision, overflow, and unsupported-currency submissions; unsafe image URLs were not linked or fetched, and injected markup remained literal text."
    },
    {
      "case": "G06-05",
      "status": "PASS",
      "reason": "Contact from the marketplace opened the correct seller conversation target without changing the displayed offer, publishing any payment/checkout/private-message event, or exposing a checkout control. The UI identifies NIP-15 as draft and states that payments/custody are not handled."
    }
